Move nitroo's GKR verifier out of the prover feature, to stwo::core::lookups.

Part of the verifier-only build of SASH eb95bfa that the SP1 segment guest runs
(verifiable-inference-ethereum SPEC.md §1.1). Upstream source is Apache-2.0;
this patch modifies it (Apache-2.0 §4(b)).

SASH's verify_composed runs a LogUp-GKR batch verification whenever
gkr_key_tiles is set, but nitroo keeps that verifier in stwo::prover::lookups,
which exists only with the prover feature; that feature needs array_chunks,
which Rust 1.90 removed, so it cannot build in an SP1 guest. The verifier half
uses only core types, so it moves to a new stwo::core::lookups:

- core/lookups/gkr_verifier.rs: everything in prover/lookups/gkr_verifier.rs
  before its tests (partially_verify_batch, GkrBatchProof, GkrArtifact, Gate,
  GkrMask, GkrError, LayerIndex);
- core/lookups/sumcheck.rs: the verifier half of prover/lookups/sumcheck.rs
  (partially_verify, SumcheckProof, MAX_DEGREE, SumcheckError, RoundIndex);
- core/lookups/utils.rs: all of prover/lookups/utils.rs, with its tests.

Function bodies are unchanged. prover/lookups/{gkr_verifier,sumcheck}.rs
re-export the moved items (`pub use crate::core::lookups::<mod>::*;`) and keep
their tests and the prover half, and prover/lookups/utils.rs becomes a
re-export, so prover-side imports compile unchanged. SASH's verifier imports
(prover/src/gkr_key_tile.rs, prover/src/gkrlink.rs) point at the new path.

